### Shelfwise sample requests (IntelliJ / VS Code REST Client)
@host = http://localhost:8080

### Login as librarian
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "librarian",
  "password": "librarian123"
}

### save the token from the response here
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### List books
GET {{host}}/api/v1/books

### Search v2
GET {{host}}/api/v2/books/search?q=code&availableOnly=true&sort=title,desc

### Check out a book
POST {{host}}/api/v1/loans/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "memberId": 1,
  "bookId": 2
}

### Return a book
POST {{host}}/api/v1/loans/1/return
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Renew a loan
POST {{host}}/api/v1/loans/1/renew
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Reserve a book
POST {{host}}/api/v1/reservations?bookId=5&memberId=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard
GET {{host}}/api/v1/reports/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Pay a fine
POST {{host}}/api/v1/fines/1/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 1.25,
  "method": "CASH"
}

### Import books from CSV
POST {{host}}/api/v1/data/import/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample-books.csv"

< ../src/main/resources/import/sample-books.csv
--boundary--
